1
00:00:19,880 --> 00:00:24,260
Anyone without money, come to me.

2
00:00:24,260 --> 00:00:28,980
I don't have any either, so don't worry.

3
00:00:28,980 --> 00:00:36,040
Look, blue skies and white clouds.

4
00:00:36,040 --> 00:00:36,440
me

5
00:00:38,860 --> 00:00:42,840
Somehow we'll get by with this place.

6
00:00:55,920 --> 00:00:59,900
Anyone without a job, come to me.

7
00:00:59,900 --> 00:01:04,500
I don't have one either, so don't worry.

8
00:01:40,960 --> 00:01:42,960
Clean off the graffiti.

9
00:01:48,280 --> 00:01:52,420
This stain looks like something.

10
00:01:52,420 --> 00:01:54,340
What was it again?

11
00:01:54,340 --> 00:01:56,020
Wait.

12
00:01:57,640 --> 00:01:59,160
It goes like this, then.

13
00:01:59,160 --> 00:02:01,160
Like this,

14
00:02:01,160 --> 00:02:04,020
connect this to over here.

15
00:02:04,500 --> 00:02:06,540
It was like this.

16
00:02:12,520 --> 00:02:15,600
Like this, like this, and then

17
00:02:16,920 --> 00:02:17,980
like this

18
00:02:18,420 --> 00:02:21,080
It's Chief Ohara's little mustache.

19
00:02:21,880 --> 00:02:23,720
That nagging, stubborn old geezer.

20
00:02:23,720 --> 00:02:25,840
Just the other day,
in front of all the parents,

21
00:02:25,840 --> 00:02:28,400
he made a complete laughingstock out of me.

22
00:02:29,020 --> 00:02:31,000
Honestly, you're such a...

23
00:02:31,000 --> 00:02:33,560
No matter how old you get,
you're still a kid.

24
00:02:34,740 --> 00:02:39,500
Why don't you act with some awareness and a sense of
responsibility befitting your position as a senior constable?

25
00:02:39,500 --> 00:02:42,460
At this rate,
you'll never get a wife in your whole life!

26
00:02:43,000 --> 00:02:45,960
Damn, just thinking
about it makes me furious.

27
00:02:45,960 --> 00:02:47,360
I'll show him like this!

28
00:02:50,740 --> 00:02:54,540
Daijiro-kun,
you had an accident, didn't you?

29
00:02:55,840 --> 00:02:57,140
Serves you right!

30
00:02:57,140 --> 00:02:59,560
Oh no, Ryo-chan, what are you writing?

31
00:03:01,960 --> 00:03:05,760
Ah, damn it! What am I doing?!

32
00:03:06,260 --> 00:03:08,780
Honestly, Ryo-chan,
you have to wipe it off properly!

33
00:03:11,047 --> 00:03:15,440
Of all things, I went and drew
it clearly with permanent marker.

34
00:03:15,740 --> 00:03:19,040
I think there was some permanent
marker remover around here somewhere.

35
00:03:19,180 --> 00:03:19,580
Thanks.

36
00:03:20,100 --> 00:03:23,960
Be careful. Haa, the day has finally come!

37
00:03:23,960 --> 00:03:26,440
Shut up! Why are you getting
so worked up all by yourself?!

38
00:03:26,840 --> 00:03:33,780
Ryo-san, that person just now was the
9,999th person I gave directions to.

39
00:03:35,180 --> 00:03:41,080
Actually, the first job I did when I came
to this station was giving directions.

40
00:03:41,780 --> 00:03:47,820
So ever since then, I've been noting down the number of people
I've guided in the corner of my logbook every single day.

41
00:03:48,280 --> 00:03:48,840
See?

42
00:03:51,220 --> 00:03:53,780
So you're the one who
wrote that 小 character?

43
00:03:53,780 --> 00:03:57,760
I've been wondering what that was for a long time,
and now the mystery's solved.

44
00:03:57,760 --> 00:03:59,460
Hey, that's not the point right now.

45
00:03:59,460 --> 00:04:01,600
Wait, Ryo-san, at least let me finish.

46
00:04:02,560 --> 00:04:07,380
So if that last person was the 9,999th,

47
00:04:07,380 --> 00:04:09,660
it's Magic 1, Ryo-san.

48
00:04:09,660 --> 00:04:10,940
Magic 1.

49
00:04:11,340 --> 00:04:13,540
that means I'll hit 10,000 people today.

50
00:04:15,360 --> 00:04:17,360
Look, Ryo-san.

51
00:04:19,420 --> 00:04:21,520
My handmade mini kusudama.

52
00:04:22,640 --> 00:04:25,760
I stayed up all night making it yesterday.

53
00:04:27,760 --> 00:04:30,460
The 10,000th person will
get to draw one of these.

54
00:04:30,460 --> 00:04:32,980
This one's a small commemorative gift.

55
00:04:32,980 --> 00:04:34,920
Are you a grade schooler or something?

56
00:04:35,540 --> 00:04:36,660
Let me take a look at that.

57
00:04:36,660 --> 00:04:38,200
What are you planning, Ryo-san?

58
00:04:39,000 --> 00:04:41,040
I'll pull it out for you.

59
00:04:41,040 --> 00:04:42,660
No way, come on.

60
00:04:42,660 --> 00:04:44,400
Come on, let me have a laugh!

61
00:04:44,400 --> 00:04:45,700
I said let me see it.

62
00:04:45,700 --> 00:04:48,520
*squish squish squish squish*

63
00:04:48,520 --> 00:04:49,460
Hahaha!

64
00:04:49,460 --> 00:04:51,900
Hey, stop it, Ryo-san!

65
00:04:52,980 --> 00:04:55,200
If you don't make me laugh,
I'll tickle you even more.

66
00:04:55,200 --> 00:04:57,800
*tickle tickle tickle*

67
00:04:57,800 --> 00:04:59,140
Stop it, stop it!

68
00:04:59,140 --> 00:05:01,800
*tickle tickle tickle tickle*

69
00:05:01,800 --> 00:05:03,260
Hahaha!

70
00:05:04,500 --> 00:05:05,660
What are you doing?

71
00:05:06,300 --> 00:05:07,020
Hahaha!

72
00:05:07,020 --> 00:05:09,640
Ryo-san, help me, help me!

73
00:05:09,640 --> 00:05:10,840
Hahaha!

74
00:05:10,840 --> 00:05:12,460
Now even Mom?

75
00:05:14,000 --> 00:05:17,280
It's your fault for making
such a stingy kusudama.

76
00:05:17,280 --> 00:05:22,600
Reiko-san, if anyone asks for directions,
leave the guiding to me, me!

77
00:05:22,600 --> 00:05:27,000
If you're looking for a gas station, it's
just past the second traffic light up ahead.

78
00:05:27,700 --> 00:05:28,320
Thanks!

79
00:05:28,320 --> 00:05:29,780
Aki

80
00:05:33,880 --> 00:05:36,200
Oh no, my 10,000th person just slipped away!

81
00:05:36,620 --> 00:05:38,880
How cute.

82
00:05:39,540 --> 00:05:41,340
Don't you start too, Reiko-san.

83
00:05:42,460 --> 00:05:43,560
Sorry.

84
00:05:44,460 --> 00:05:47,420
Anyway,
I'll handle the next direction request.

85
00:05:47,420 --> 00:05:50,900
And please stop trying to break my kusudama.

86
00:05:51,340 --> 00:05:51,740
That's all!

87
00:05:52,380 --> 00:05:54,640
Getting so worked up
over such a small thing.

88
00:05:55,320 --> 00:05:58,600
What was I just about to do?

89
00:06:01,060 --> 00:06:02,280
Could you keep it down a little?

90
00:06:06,200 --> 00:06:07,400
This is terrible!

91
00:06:07,700 --> 00:06:10,420
I've never heard of a cat
collapsing in the street.

92
00:06:12,620 --> 00:06:14,220
I wonder how long it's been out here.

93
00:06:14,220 --> 00:06:16,040
I had no idea.

94
00:06:16,700 --> 00:06:19,140
Poor thing, it's so limp.

95
00:06:19,520 --> 00:06:21,220
Maybe it's hungry.

96
00:06:21,220 --> 00:06:23,180
This one's way too fat.

97
00:06:23,180 --> 00:06:25,660
Shouldn't it go on a diet?

98
00:06:26,240 --> 00:06:27,480
We have some milk, right?

99
00:06:29,980 --> 00:06:33,120
Reiko isn't planning
to keep it here, is she?

100
00:06:33,120 --> 00:06:36,060
Once it's feeling better,
we can look for an owner.

101
00:06:36,060 --> 00:06:37,040
Ryo-chan

102
00:06:39,200 --> 00:06:40,100
Did someone call me?

103
00:06:40,100 --> 00:06:42,280
Ugh, you smell like a man already.

104
00:06:42,760 --> 00:06:46,040
Well, obviously!
Don't go denying my gender now, too!

105
00:06:46,040 --> 00:06:48,820
You still haven't folded up the futon for napping,
have you?

106
00:06:48,820 --> 00:06:51,420
This isn't your room, Ryo-chan, you know.

107
00:06:51,420 --> 00:06:55,000
Look, the poor kitty is suffering!

108
00:06:55,800 --> 00:06:58,240
Yes, yes, my apologies.

109
00:06:58,780 --> 00:07:00,980
Once you're done with that,
tidy up the trash too, okay?

110
00:07:00,980 --> 00:07:04,640
Sort it properly into burnable
and non-burnable trash, got it?

111
00:07:05,260 --> 00:07:06,400
I know, I know.

112
00:07:06,880 --> 00:07:08,480
I'm going to give you some milk now, okay?

113
00:07:10,100 --> 00:07:12,687
Honestly, who do you think I am?

114
00:07:12,737 --> 00:07:15,960
When it comes to sorting trash,
nobody's better than me...

115
00:07:15,960 --> 00:07:19,540
You've got a suspiciously big belly.

116
00:07:19,960 --> 00:07:20,600
Nyaa!

117
00:07:21,380 --> 00:07:23,260
What are you doing?!

118
00:07:24,040 --> 00:07:25,760
We're almost there, so hang in there.

119
00:07:26,060 --> 00:07:26,700
Chief!

120
00:07:26,980 --> 00:07:27,340
What?

121
00:07:28,300 --> 00:07:29,580
Ow ow.

122
00:07:29,740 --> 00:07:30,660
What's wrong, Chief?

123
00:07:30,900 --> 00:07:33,160
Apparently Chief Ohara has lumbago.

124
00:07:34,980 --> 00:07:35,980
This is terrible!

125
00:07:36,560 --> 00:07:39,060
Aaah, ouch, ouch.

126
00:07:39,740 --> 00:07:43,040
Oh no, I forgot to erase the graffiti!

127
00:07:44,080 --> 00:07:47,500
Geez, don't startle me like that, Ryo-chan.

128
00:07:48,680 --> 00:07:49,400
Uh-oh.

129
00:07:49,880 --> 00:07:50,960
What's wrong?

130
00:07:51,160 --> 00:07:54,600
Let me say it quickly.
Look, it's acting strange!

131
00:07:54,600 --> 00:07:56,460
Right, we need to give it some milk.

132
00:07:59,080 --> 00:08:03,060
Ugh, guh you've got the wrong number.
Hello? Hello? Hello?

133
00:08:03,060 --> 00:08:05,460
Hello, this is Kameari Park-mae Police Box.

134
00:08:05,460 --> 00:08:07,746
Aye, aye, aye, aye.

135
00:08:07,796 --> 00:08:09,900
No, damn it, it won't come out.

136
00:08:11,300 --> 00:08:12,840
Police box, check.

137
00:08:16,940 --> 00:08:20,360
Aw, no,
it's lost its stickiness and won't stick.

138
00:08:20,360 --> 00:08:21,640
What am I supposed to do?

139
00:08:21,640 --> 00:08:23,340
It's not a call for me.

140
00:08:23,340 --> 00:08:24,960
No, it isn't.

141
00:08:25,840 --> 00:08:26,560
I see.

142
00:08:27,280 --> 00:08:30,100
Nakagawa, could you lower my chair a little?

143
00:08:30,640 --> 00:08:31,040
Yes.

144
00:08:32,760 --> 00:08:33,120
Thank you.

145
00:08:33,660 --> 00:08:36,200
How did you end up with lumbago, Chief?

146
00:08:37,480 --> 00:08:38,700
Yesterday.

147
00:08:39,940 --> 00:08:43,240
I carelessly strained myself while
rearranging the bonsai in the garden.

148
00:08:44,720 --> 00:08:46,940
It wasn't even a heavy pot, either.

149
00:08:48,720 --> 00:08:49,440
Are you alright?

150
00:08:49,940 --> 00:08:51,820
Then you must be having a
lot of trouble getting around.

151
00:08:53,760 --> 00:08:56,600
Nakagawa, could I get a cup of tea?

152
00:08:57,080 --> 00:08:57,440
Yes.

153
00:08:57,440 --> 00:08:57,780
Yes.

154
00:09:00,220 --> 00:09:03,200
We can't just keep standing
around like this, can we.

155
00:09:03,780 --> 00:09:04,300
Right.

156
00:09:04,820 --> 00:09:08,360
Chief, why don't you rest in
the break room in the back?

157
00:09:08,800 --> 00:09:10,420
Yes, let's do that.

158
00:09:10,940 --> 00:09:11,800
Yeah, I suppose.

159
00:09:12,400 --> 00:09:15,100
Now, do take it easy and rest.

160
00:09:15,100 --> 00:09:16,800
She seems to be pregnant!

161
00:09:17,540 --> 00:09:17,800
What?

162
00:09:17,800 --> 00:09:22,980
Sorry, my hand slipped.

163
00:09:25,420 --> 00:09:26,460
Oh my.

164
00:09:28,960 --> 00:09:31,420
Should I make some tea?

165
00:09:31,420 --> 00:09:32,400
Please do.

166
00:09:35,680 --> 00:09:39,280
Whose kid is she carrying, then?

167
00:09:39,280 --> 00:09:41,040
Well, that's

168
00:09:41,040 --> 00:09:42,920
you don't know?

169
00:09:43,480 --> 00:09:45,140
Ow

170
00:09:45,140 --> 00:09:48,660
Chief, the one who's pregnant isn't Reiko.

171
00:09:48,660 --> 00:09:50,180
It's the cat, the cat!

172
00:09:50,880 --> 00:09:51,400
The cat?

173
00:09:54,100 --> 00:09:55,080
That cat?

174
00:09:55,080 --> 00:09:57,480
She was collapsed in
front of the police box.

175
00:09:58,920 --> 00:10:00,240
Poor thing.

176
00:10:00,980 --> 00:10:05,120
So at the very least, I want to let
her give birth quietly in this room.

177
00:10:06,420 --> 00:10:07,200
Understood.

178
00:10:07,660 --> 00:10:09,680
Ryotsu, move your chair back.

179
00:10:10,500 --> 00:10:11,720
But, Chief,

180
00:10:12,300 --> 00:10:15,200
the break room is off-limits to men today.

181
00:10:15,200 --> 00:10:17,380
Move your chair, Ryotsu.

182
00:10:18,320 --> 00:10:18,720
Yes.

183
00:10:21,600 --> 00:10:22,660
Thank you, Chief.

184
00:10:22,980 --> 00:10:24,120
Sorry.

185
00:10:25,620 --> 00:10:29,060
There's something I really
want the Chief to see.

186
00:10:29,060 --> 00:10:31,180
Now, which one was it?

187
00:10:32,980 --> 00:10:34,500
Someone seems to have come in.

188
00:10:35,200 --> 00:10:36,420
Don't worry about it.

189
00:10:36,420 --> 00:10:39,000
Hey, anyone who's free!

190
00:10:39,960 --> 00:10:40,440
Yes.

191
00:10:41,180 --> 00:10:41,900
What's wrong?

192
00:10:45,660 --> 00:10:48,560
Is there some problem with this file?

193
00:10:48,560 --> 00:10:50,900
That's a serious problem, though.

194
00:10:51,440 --> 00:10:57,860
Take the second corner on the left, then the next corner on the right, and you'll find it right away.
Thank you very much.

195
00:10:59,600 --> 00:11:01,580
My 10,000th one.

196
00:11:03,800 --> 00:11:06,000
Be quiet, or you'll startle the cat.

197
00:11:06,500 --> 00:11:07,500
Sorry.

198
00:11:10,000 --> 00:11:11,400
Here you go, Chief.

199
00:11:11,900 --> 00:11:12,340
Thanks.

200
00:11:13,320 --> 00:11:16,260
So what exactly is this 10,000th thing?

201
00:11:16,900 --> 00:11:21,720
It's the number of people Terai has given directions
to since he started working at this station.

202
00:11:22,240 --> 00:11:22,680
Wow.

203
00:11:22,680 --> 00:11:25,920
Terai, you've given
directions to 10,000 citizens?

204
00:11:28,500 --> 00:11:32,140
As long as there are diligent,
steady officers like Terai,

205
00:11:32,140 --> 00:11:37,480
Katsushika's peace is secure.
Even though I didn't know, I'm sorry.

206
00:11:38,000 --> 00:11:45,620
He's just doing this on his own, so no need to apologize.
Yeah, I'm just thinking it on my own.

207
00:11:46,300 --> 00:11:50,680
Next time,
I'll be sure to tell Terai. Thanks.

208
00:11:54,520 --> 00:11:57,700
Staring at these bookshelves
all the time is suffocating.

209
00:11:57,700 --> 00:12:01,080
Let's look at this file again another time.

210
00:12:01,080 --> 00:12:02,920
I see. Then...

211
00:12:03,940 --> 00:12:05,060
How about this?

212
00:12:05,660 --> 00:12:06,060
Thank you.

213
00:12:07,540 --> 00:12:12,280
As long as I've got breath in my body, I never thought I'd need your help,
but...

214
00:12:12,840 --> 00:12:16,240
Aw, Chief, just tell me anything you need.

215
00:12:16,240 --> 00:12:18,380
Don't be so distant, come on.

216
00:12:21,260 --> 00:12:21,920
Found it.

217
00:12:25,020 --> 00:12:29,000
Let me stay here for a while
until a call comes in for me.

218
00:12:31,900 --> 00:12:35,380
I'll wait here on standby so they
can install the phone right away.

219
00:12:35,380 --> 00:12:37,740
Rest assured, Chief.

220
00:12:37,740 --> 00:12:39,360
Thanks. Sorry about this.

221
00:12:41,920 --> 00:12:45,360
Damn it, what am I supposed to do?

222
00:12:59,140 --> 00:13:01,060
That's a magnificent black pine, Chief.

223
00:13:02,380 --> 00:13:03,240
You think so?

224
00:13:03,660 --> 00:13:07,640
My father has an acquaintance who serves
as a director of the bonsai association,

225
00:13:08,160 --> 00:13:10,780
and I've heard him talk about
the hardships of cultivating them.

226
00:13:11,700 --> 00:13:13,680
Growing one with branches this well-shaped

227
00:13:14,000 --> 00:13:15,940
is no ordinary feat, is it?

228
00:13:16,940 --> 00:13:20,320
Yes, it took me ten years
to raise it to this point.

229
00:13:20,320 --> 00:13:21,040
Ten years?

230
00:13:21,560 --> 00:13:24,600
Ryo-san,
the chief's bonsai photo is right here.

231
00:13:25,160 --> 00:13:27,200
What a fine shape it has.

232
00:13:27,200 --> 00:13:30,280
There's no way you'd know
anything about branch shape.

233
00:13:30,280 --> 00:13:34,560
You probably think bonsai is just something idle old men do,
don't you?

234
00:13:36,160 --> 00:13:38,640
Normally I'd talk back right about now,

235
00:13:38,640 --> 00:13:41,000
but I've got weaknesses of my own,
after all.

236
00:13:41,000 --> 00:13:42,520
Let's keep the peace here.

237
00:13:42,980 --> 00:13:45,060
No way, Chief.

238
00:13:45,940 --> 00:13:48,375
Ever since I saw your bonsai at your house,

239
00:13:48,425 --> 00:13:54,060
I've secretly been hoping to
take up bonsai as a hobby someday.

240
00:13:55,740 --> 00:13:56,540
Really?

241
00:13:57,300 --> 00:14:00,757
Senpai has nimble hands and
is good at fine detail work,

242
00:14:00,807 --> 00:14:03,480
so he might actually be suited to it.

243
00:14:03,700 --> 00:14:05,560
As long as he fixes
that short temper of his.

244
00:14:05,800 --> 00:14:06,340
Shut up!

245
00:14:13,700 --> 00:14:18,780
Actually, I entered this bonsai
in today's bonsai exhibition.

246
00:14:19,400 --> 00:14:20,500
I see.

247
00:14:21,180 --> 00:14:24,000
My wife went to the venue on my behalf.

248
00:14:24,440 --> 00:14:28,100
They're supposed to call here
as soon as the results are known.

249
00:14:28,640 --> 00:14:32,500
So the call you've been
waiting for is from your wife?

250
00:14:32,500 --> 00:14:32,920
Yes.

251
00:14:32,920 --> 00:14:34,740
I'm getting so nervous.

252
00:14:37,060 --> 00:14:41,800
Looking back, these past ten years
have been a true battle with myself.

253
00:14:42,460 --> 00:14:46,980
This bonsai is, so to speak,
an extension of myself.

254
00:14:48,060 --> 00:14:52,120
When I think of that extension
now being judged by others...

255
00:14:52,120 --> 00:14:53,960
I can't sit still...

256
00:14:53,960 --> 00:14:55,920
Ow ow ow!

257
00:14:55,920 --> 00:14:57,640
Are you all right, Chief?

258
00:14:57,640 --> 00:15:01,080
Good things come to those who wait,
Chief, as they say.

259
00:15:01,580 --> 00:15:05,800
If you can't go to the venue anyway,
you should just stay home and rest quietly.

260
00:15:06,340 --> 00:15:08,720
It doesn't matter where you take the call,
does it?

261
00:15:10,380 --> 00:15:12,580
Waiting alone at home is hard.

262
00:15:12,580 --> 00:15:14,160
I understand how you feel.

263
00:15:14,160 --> 00:15:16,880
It's like being a student preparing for exams again,
isn't it?

264
00:15:17,360 --> 00:15:18,160
Yeah, it is.

265
00:15:18,880 --> 00:15:19,840
It's miserable, you know.

266
00:15:19,840 --> 00:15:22,720
Staying here keeps your mind off things.

267
00:15:24,380 --> 00:15:27,200
If the Chief keeps sitting here like this,

268
00:15:27,200 --> 00:15:30,060
we really have to do something
about the graffiti on the wall.

269
00:15:30,940 --> 00:15:33,340
But I can't handle it alone.

270
00:15:33,340 --> 00:15:34,840
I need reinforcements.

271
00:15:36,340 --> 00:15:37,620
The bigwigs are no help.

272
00:15:38,340 --> 00:15:41,280
Poking the snake would just
get us caught by the Chief.

273
00:15:43,040 --> 00:15:46,780
In that case,
we have no choice but to rope in Nakagawa.

274
00:15:51,100 --> 00:15:52,540
What is it? Sonbol?

275
00:15:56,540 --> 00:15:57,500
What's wrong?

276
00:15:58,880 --> 00:16:02,060
There's a cardboard box on
top of the locker, right?

277
00:16:02,640 --> 00:16:03,720
Could you grab that for me?

278
00:16:04,560 --> 00:16:07,580
Are you going to clean it
with the cleaning detergent?

279
00:16:12,020 --> 00:16:15,640
Senpai, what are you writing?

280
00:16:15,640 --> 00:16:18,640
The full story of how I
ended up writing this can wait.

281
00:16:18,640 --> 00:16:21,500
I want to erase this
before the Chief notices.

282
00:16:21,500 --> 00:16:22,700
Help me out.

283
00:16:26,260 --> 00:16:27,920
There's no way I can do that.

284
00:16:28,900 --> 00:16:31,560
All I need is for you to grab
the box on top of the locker.

285
00:16:31,560 --> 00:16:32,520
Please.

286
00:16:33,800 --> 00:16:35,080
It's just grabbing the box, that's all.

287
00:16:35,720 --> 00:16:37,700
What are you two whispering about?

288
00:16:39,220 --> 00:16:41,460
While we wait for your wife to call,

289
00:16:41,460 --> 00:16:43,600
so the Chief doesn't get bored,

290
00:16:43,600 --> 00:16:47,100
we were talking about some
good way to pass the time.

291
00:16:47,700 --> 00:16:50,280
Ryotsu, you really are something else.

292
00:16:51,400 --> 00:16:52,000
Now!

293
00:16:59,680 --> 00:17:01,620
What's that way you're holding it?

294
00:17:04,300 --> 00:17:05,120
Sorry.

295
00:17:06,440 --> 00:17:08,020
What, are you cleaning or something?

296
00:17:09,200 --> 00:17:10,860
No, it's just that, well...

297
00:17:11,720 --> 00:17:14,720
Nakagawa, you klutz,
what's with that weird movement?

298
00:17:14,720 --> 00:17:18,400
If the Chief notices,
we can't be erasing graffiti here!

299
00:17:19,560 --> 00:17:22,920
If there's anything I can do, just say so.
I'll help you!

300
00:17:22,920 --> 00:17:24,160
I see.

301
00:17:27,520 --> 00:17:31,400
I chose the wrong person. Terai would've been
much better suited for this sort of thing.

302
00:17:31,400 --> 00:17:34,000
But it's too late to regret it now.

303
00:17:35,040 --> 00:17:35,540
That's it!

304
00:17:38,040 --> 00:17:38,860
This is it.

305
00:17:41,680 --> 00:17:44,200
Chief, I've got something good.

306
00:17:44,200 --> 00:17:46,400
Let's play shogi, shogi.

307
00:17:46,400 --> 00:17:48,940
But you're on duty, aren't you?

308
00:17:50,080 --> 00:17:52,260
Terai and Nakagawa are here too,

309
00:17:52,260 --> 00:17:54,400
and it's not like we're going anywhere.

310
00:17:54,400 --> 00:17:56,080
Isn't it fine once in a while?

311
00:17:56,080 --> 00:17:57,780
Come on, Chief, let's play.

312
00:17:57,780 --> 00:18:01,040
Well, I suppose it would
help take my mind off things.

313
00:18:01,400 --> 00:18:02,160
Fine, let's do it.

314
00:18:14,960 --> 00:18:17,120
I'll go first.

315
00:18:26,580 --> 00:18:28,020
So that's your move.

316
00:18:39,500 --> 00:18:41,100
It's your turn, Ryotsu.

317
00:18:51,340 --> 00:18:55,200
Before coming here, I got a handshake
from actress Sayuri Yoshikawa,

318
00:18:55,200 --> 00:18:57,880
so I don't want to touch anyone else today.

319
00:19:01,880 --> 00:19:02,960
What's with you all of a sudden?

320
00:19:04,900 --> 00:19:07,880
So that's why you've been acting
suspicious this whole time?

321
00:19:13,180 --> 00:19:15,160
But it's Sayuri Yoshikawa!

322
00:19:15,160 --> 00:19:16,940
You almost never get to meet her.

323
00:19:17,480 --> 00:19:19,540
I wish I could have seen her,
even just once.

324
00:19:20,220 --> 00:19:22,820
They were filming near Katsushika Station.

325
00:19:24,100 --> 00:19:26,780
I've been a fan since way back,
so she shook my hand.

326
00:19:27,600 --> 00:19:29,360
Are you a middle schooler or something?

327
00:19:30,540 --> 00:19:32,200
I've never been told
that by a senior officer.

328
00:19:33,460 --> 00:19:34,800
Somehow, that's reassuring.

329
00:19:34,800 --> 00:19:37,420
Whenever I hear that kind
of thing about Nakagawa,

330
00:19:37,420 --> 00:19:38,600
yeah, it's true.

331
00:19:39,180 --> 00:19:41,280
even Nakagawa, who seems flawless,

332
00:19:41,280 --> 00:19:43,300
turns out to be just as
ordinary as anyone else.

333
00:19:44,340 --> 00:19:45,680
Please don't tease me.

334
00:19:46,200 --> 00:19:47,760
Hey, everyone!

335
00:19:49,420 --> 00:19:51,000
They've been born!

336
00:19:51,000 --> 00:19:52,620
I see.

337
00:19:56,300 --> 00:19:57,360
They're so tiny.

338
00:19:57,360 --> 00:19:58,840
They're adorable.

339
00:19:59,500 --> 00:20:00,580
Good work.

340
00:20:01,060 --> 00:20:02,900
No, I didn't do anything.

341
00:20:03,440 --> 00:20:05,680
The mother cat did it all by herself.

342
00:20:05,680 --> 00:20:08,020
I just watched from nearby.

343
00:20:14,840 --> 00:20:17,900
This oil-based cleaner

344
00:20:17,900 --> 00:20:19,120
This one?

345
00:20:19,120 --> 00:20:21,480
It's oddly light.

346
00:20:27,420 --> 00:20:28,720
Excuse me.

347
00:20:29,720 --> 00:20:31,020
That road...

348
00:20:31,020 --> 00:20:33,100
Terai, you've got a visitor!

349
00:20:36,300 --> 00:20:37,500
The 10,000th person!

350
00:20:37,500 --> 00:20:39,860
Looks like you're finally
reaching the milestone.

351
00:20:39,860 --> 00:20:41,000
Terai-san

352
00:20:42,240 --> 00:20:43,140
What's going on?

353
00:20:46,420 --> 00:20:47,620
This way, this way!

354
00:20:49,700 --> 00:20:50,880
Excuse me.

355
00:20:50,880 --> 00:20:53,820
Where's the big Shibamata-san exhibition?

356
00:20:55,040 --> 00:20:55,480
No way.

357
00:20:56,000 --> 00:20:58,520
To think there are ten 10,000th visitors!

358
00:20:59,080 --> 00:21:00,460
What are we supposed to do?

359
00:21:01,360 --> 00:21:06,260
If it's a large store, you'd better get
off at the next station, Kanamachi, and walk.

360
00:21:06,260 --> 00:21:07,400
Understood.

361
00:21:10,540 --> 00:21:11,560
They're gone.

362
00:21:12,340 --> 00:21:16,720
I'm starting to feel like I won't
reach the 10,000-visitor record.

363
00:21:17,740 --> 00:21:19,100
Isn't it just one more person?

364
00:21:19,500 --> 00:21:22,620
Let's put off the complicated
cases and wait for the next one.

365
00:21:22,620 --> 00:21:23,640
Yeah, you're right.

366
00:21:23,640 --> 00:21:24,780
Don't leave me behind!

367
00:21:26,200 --> 00:21:27,280
What, Ryo-san?

368
00:21:28,560 --> 00:21:31,680
Where's the closest convenience
store around here again?

369
00:21:31,680 --> 00:21:35,280
Then this mart that just
opened last week is close.

370
00:21:35,280 --> 00:21:38,340
About 200 meters down this road,
on the left side.

371
00:21:38,340 --> 00:21:38,800
Thanks.

372
00:21:43,800 --> 00:21:45,400
What are you doing, Ryo-san?

373
00:21:45,400 --> 00:21:49,400
That's why you should have just let
Bokuchan break it honestly from the start.

374
00:21:49,800 --> 00:21:53,340
I don't want Ryo-san to
be the 10,000th person!

375
00:21:55,700 --> 00:21:56,880
Eeeeeeh!

376
00:22:01,100 --> 00:22:06,360
Hello? Yes, that's right.
Please hold on a moment.

377
00:22:06,780 --> 00:22:09,300
Chief, it's your wife.

378
00:22:10,440 --> 00:22:11,140
I see.

379
00:22:16,140 --> 00:22:19,060
Hello, this is Hashida.

380
00:22:19,060 --> 00:22:22,360
I see.

381
00:22:22,360 --> 00:22:23,740
Understood.

382
00:22:28,860 --> 00:22:31,300
Chief, the result is in.

383
00:22:32,280 --> 00:22:33,920
You came in second place, apparently.

384
00:22:33,920 --> 00:22:35,760
That's runner-up!

385
00:22:35,760 --> 00:22:37,500
That's amazing, Chief!

386
00:22:37,500 --> 00:22:38,920
Congratulations!

387
00:22:42,860 --> 00:22:44,300
What are you talking about?

388
00:22:45,100 --> 00:22:45,780
Thank you.

389
00:22:46,920 --> 00:22:47,600
Thank you.

390
00:22:47,600 --> 00:22:48,120
Thank you.

391
00:22:50,780 --> 00:22:56,880
Ahaha, I'll let Nakagawa
off the handshake today.

392
00:22:57,300 --> 00:22:58,200
No, Chief.

393
00:22:59,500 --> 00:23:00,600
Congratulations!

394
00:23:01,220 --> 00:23:03,780
An indirect handshake with
Sayuri Yoshikawa Chief?

395
00:23:04,940 --> 00:23:07,060
Right, I'm not washing this hand today!

396
00:23:08,260 --> 00:23:10,200
What about Sayuri Yoshikawa?

397
00:23:10,920 --> 00:23:12,900
I've gained a new respect for you, Ryotsu.

398
00:23:12,900 --> 00:23:16,640
Stop it, you're embarrassing me, Chief.

399
00:23:17,740 --> 00:23:19,760
I can't show that to anyone anymore.

400
00:23:20,100 --> 00:23:23,580
You stuck right by my side all
day and took good care of me.

401
00:23:24,600 --> 00:23:24,980
Thank you.

402
00:23:25,460 --> 00:23:28,385
Chief, what's wrong?
You're not acting like yourself.

403
00:23:28,435 --> 00:23:29,600
Stop it, please.

404
00:23:29,780 --> 00:23:33,480
I've never found your presence
so reassuring as I did today.

405
00:23:34,200 --> 00:23:34,580
Thank you.

406
00:23:39,260 --> 00:23:41,460
Only you would draw something like this!

407
00:23:43,900 --> 00:23:50,500
So that's why you stuck close, to hide this!
Hey, Ryo-chan, you still haven't erased this morning's graffiti?

408
00:23:50,500 --> 00:23:53,880
Chief, there are a lot of
circumstances behind this...

409
00:23:55,080 --> 00:23:56,620
Idiot!

410
00:23:56,620 --> 00:24:01,460
What happened to your lumbago, Chief?

411
00:24:15,100 --> 00:24:20,520
An afternoon after the rain,
as if someone is calling

412
00:24:21,720 --> 00:24:27,140
Walking while looking back,
led by the hand of the gacha

413
00:24:28,260 --> 00:24:34,300
That strange feeling I had back then

414
00:24:35,120 --> 00:24:39,540
So, on the arcade's tiles,

415
00:24:39,540 --> 00:24:45,320
I tried walking only on the black ones

416
00:24:47,880 --> 00:24:53,620
Everyone was a child once,
but everyone has forgotten

417
00:24:54,560 --> 00:24:57,640
Not the politicians with
their self-important faces

418
00:24:57,640 --> 00:25:00,980
Nor the aunties with blue eyeshadow

419
00:25:00,980 --> 00:25:06,600
Try turning at that corner

420
00:25:07,720 --> 00:25:11,760
You can meet everyone, everyone

421
00:25:12,300 --> 00:25:16,340
Over there is Kame-ari

422
00:25:17,400 --> 00:25:19,680
Well, surely Kameari...

423
00:25:21,100 --> 00:25:24,860
Everyone, come to our town!

424
00:25:25,860 --> 00:25:26,440
Thank you.

425
00:25:29,880 --> 00:25:32,860
When it comes to Grandma's Harajuku,
it's Sugamo.

426
00:25:32,860 --> 00:25:35,100
But for Grandpa, there's nothing at all.

427
00:25:36,920 --> 00:25:38,960
Let's make Kameari Grandpa's flower academy.

428
00:25:38,960 --> 00:25:41,100
Reviving the town is a wholesale plan.

429
00:25:41,100 --> 00:25:43,460
Isn't this a wonderful plan,
if I do say so myself?

430
00:25:43,460 --> 00:25:46,380
Next time: Ryotsu Town Remodeling Plan

431
00:25:46,820 --> 00:25:47,540
See you then.

432
00:25:52,700 --> 00:25:53,060
Thank you.

